KG42.register("rules-53aea9f0cb36aeeee54daa35",{"id":"42-data_center_space_time_flexibility::v141-c-R016","paper":"42-data_center_space_time_flexibility","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R016","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M05","name":"Supply submission","process_stage":"bidding","market_meaning":"The supplier submits a bid price and offered capacity at each time node. Scope: Supplier bids across the time horizon in the temporal virtual-link model with a single spatial node and no transmission network.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function bidding.supply under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.supply"],"E":[],"omega":{"market_type":"DEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"bidding","context_text":"Supplier bids across the time horizon in the temporal virtual-link model with a single spatial node and no transmission network.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e033"]},"x":[],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R016-TH001","symbol":"\\alpha^{p}_{t}","meaning":"Supplier's bid price at time node t in the temporal virtual-link market with a single spatial node and no transmission network.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"supplier-submitted bid price; no numeric value is specified in the supplied temporal bidding passage"},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e033","v141-b-g03-E06"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R016-TH002","symbol":"\\bar p_{t}","meaning":"Supplier's offered capacity at time node t in the temporal virtual-link market with a single spatial node and no transmission network.","value":{"kind":"symbolic","number_value":null,"text_value":"supplier-submitted offered capacity; no numeric value is specified in the supplied temporal bidding passage"},"unit":null,"indices":["t"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e033","v141-b-g03-E06"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R016-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The supplier submits a bid price and offered capacity at each time node. Scope: Supplier bids across the time horizon in the temporal virtual-link model with a single spatial node and no transmission network.","expression":"\\forall t\\in\\mathcal{T}:\\ \\text{supplier submits bid }(\\alpha^{p}_{t},\\bar p_{t}).","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R016-TH001","v141-c-R016-TH002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e033","v141-b-g03-E06"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e033","location":{"location_id":"src-1c03246cb9-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M05-participation","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.6 Basic formulation with general virtual links (temporal)","anchor_text":"model, we consider a time horizon given by the time nodes  = te {𝑡1, 𝑡2, … , 𝑡𝑇}. For simplicity, w","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"To see how to incorporate temporal virtual links in the clearing model, we consider a time horizon given by the time nodes T=\\{t_1,t_2,\\ldots,t_T\\}. For simplicity, we consider a network with a single spatial node (no transmission network is present in this setting). For each time node t\\in T, the DaCe bids a price \\alpha^{d}_t and a capacity \\bar d_t that represents the amount of load requested. Similarly, we consider a supplier that bids a price \\alpha^{p}_t and a capacity \\bar p_t at time t\\in T. The clearing formulation will find optimal levels for load satisfaction d_t and generation p_t for each time t\\in T."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E06","location":{"location_id":"src-1c03246cb9-p08-c1r4__v141-a-M05-bidding","page":8,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.6 Basic formulation with general virtual links (temporal)","anchor_text":"model, we consider a time horizon given by the time nodes  = te {𝑡1, 𝑡2, … , 𝑡𝑇}. For simplicity, w","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-08.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"For each time node t\\in\\mathcal{T}, the DaCe bids a price \\alpha^d_t and a capacity \\bar{d}_t that represents the amount of load requested. Similarly, we consider a supplier that bids a price \\alpha^p_t and a capacity \\bar{p}_t at time t\\in\\mathcal{T}. The clearing formulation will find optimal levels for load satisfaction d_t and generation p_t for each time t\\in\\mathcal{T}.\nEach virtual link v\\in\\mathcal{V} branches from a time node t to a later time node t'. The virtual link bids into the market at a price \\alpha^\\delta_v and capacity \\delta_t. The load at each time t\\in\\mathcal{T} is associated with a set of virtual links \\mathcal{V}_t\\subseteq\\mathcal{V}. For each v\\in\\mathcal{V}_t, we have snd(v)=t (since each consumer can only bid flexibility going from the current time to a later time). The market clearing process will find the optimal time shift flows \\delta_v for each v\\in\\mathcal{V}. A distinguishing feature of temporal virtual links (compared to spatial virtual links) is that they are naturally unidirectional."}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":"C explicitly supplied only source-backed unary facts for this function; other graph gaps remain reviewable.","empty_x_reason":"The source introduces alpha^p_t and p_bar_t as supplier bid data for the temporal market-clearing problem; the cleared generation p_t belongs to the clearing formulation, not to this supply-submission rule. No design or operational decision variable is supported for this rule, so x is empty.","empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M05-bidding","v141-a-M05-participation"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"bidding.supply","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e033","quote":"Similarly, we consider a supplier that bids a price \\alpha^{p}_t and a capacity \\bar p_t at time t\\in T."}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"a624f896c2c36c325fe523326ce6d2a4ac4df878a2adad2b0960369ebebb989e","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The supplied temporal passage explicitly states that, at each time node t in the time horizon, a supplier bids a bid price alpha^p_t and an offered capacity p_bar_t. These are bid data for the temporal single-spatial-node market and are formalized as parameters of the frozen bidding.supply fact. The evidence remains unreviewed candidate support, so this is a provisional formalization only.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-TH001","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The bid price alpha^p_t is part of the supplier bid submission represented by the frozen bidding.supply node. The frozen graph has no edges for this rule."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-TH002","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The offered capacity p_bar_t is part of the supplier bid submission represented by the frozen bidding.supply node. The frozen graph has no edges for this rule."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R016-C001","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":[],"rationale":"The formalized supply-submission declaration is attached to the frozen bidding.supply node; no edge is present in the frozen rule graph."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
